From d48983dedd363d693dfc3ed8cd8d8ef48600c8f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:22:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: wait for an unmapped SMP2P boot state on
 no-reset devices

Gaokun3 boot diagnostics show PAS reading an unmapped SMP2P entry and
returning -ENODEV, followed 4.589 ms later by an inbound ready/handover
sample. The IRQ provider can be bound while its remote state entry is
still unavailable.

On no-reset devices, retry only this unavailable-state error in
sleepable probe context with a 100 ms monotonic budget and 5-10 ms
sleeps. Read all four levels again on each attempt. The mapped-state
fast path and reset-capable startup have no added wait. Stop immediately
on a valid state or any other error; retain terminal errors and
fatal/stop checks. No firmware reset, forced attachment or indefinite
deferred probing is introduced.

Keep the diagnostic samples and report retry count, elapsed time and
final read result. This covers the observed provider/consumer race
without assuming that a delay alone makes the remote processor ready.

Signed-off-by: zhzy0077 <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index 635a44a..335d945 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -1,98 +1,101 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 /*
